   "html_text": "Allchin (1996, 2007), Weber (2002), and Matlin (2016) analyze an important reconstitution experiment at the interface of cell biology and biochemistry that played a major role in resolving a conflict between two opposing accounts of the synthesis of ATP in oxidative metabolism. Biochemists spent a couple decades trying to identify a purely chemical pathway that used the energy released in oxidative metabolism to synthesize ATP (as happens in glycolysis). Peter Mitchell (1961) advanced an alterna",
